# An Introduction to Genetic Algorithms and to Their Use in Information Retrieval.

**Authors:** Jones, Gareth, And Others

## Abstract
Genetic algorithms, a class of nondeterministic algorithms in which the role of chance makes the precise nature of a solution impossible to guarantee, seem to be well suited to combinatorial-optimization problems in information retrieval. Provides an introduction to techniques and characteristics of genetic algorithms and illustrates their operation in several textual information retrieval problems. (PEN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ532941

